    }
   ],
   "surprises": [
    {
     "claim": "Chip-grade silicon must be at least about nine nines (99.9999999 percent) pure, roughly one foreign atom per billion, with top grades even purer.",
     "role": "stakes",
     "search": "electronic grade silicon purity nine nines one atom per billion"
    },
    {
     "claim": "Silicon is made by heating quartz with carbon in an electric arc furnace at up to about 2,000 °C (industry ranges run from roughly 1,500 or 1,300 °C up to 2,000 °C).",
     "role": "fix2",
     "search": "metallurgical silicon arc furnace quartz carbon 2000 C"
    },
    {
     "claim": "A single modern chip can hold over 20 billion transistors.",
     "role": "fact",
     "search": "chip transistor count over 20 billion"
    }
   ]
  },
  "sentences": [
   {
    "role": "hook",
    "text": "If you dig a pit and let muddy water settle, you have a sandy floor."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem",
    "text": "But sand is silicon locked to oxygen, so no current passes through it."
   },
   {
    "role": "stakes",
    "text": "It is full of clay and iron, yet a chip allows only one foreign atom per billion."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix1",
    "text": "So you pour the sand into a furnace with carbon."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix2",
    "text": "Then you heat it to about 2,000 degrees Celsius, and the oxygen burns off as gas."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix3",
    "text": "So you melt the pure silicon and pull one single crystal out of it."
   },
   {
    "role": "name",
    "text": "This is a Czochralski crystal puller."
   },
   {
    "role": "name2",
    "text": "Slice the crystal into thin discs, and each disc is a wafer."
   },
   {
    "role": "how",
    "text": "Machines print layer after layer of tiny switches onto each wafer with light."
   },
   {
    "role": "fact",
    "text": "One modern chip can hold over 20 billion of those switches."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem2",
    "text": "But a single speck of dust landing on a wafer can kill the chip."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem3",
    "text": "And out in the open, rain blows mud onto the machines and ruins a whole batch."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix4",
    "text": "So you build a hall around the machines and push filtered air down, making a cleanroom."
   },
   {
    "role": "finish",
    "text": "Add ceiling lights over the machines, and the pit water runs clear."
   },
   {
    "role": "congrats",
    "text": "Congratulations, you have built a semiconductor factory."
   }
  ],
